From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:10:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10214/11362] Retract 122 more stale stamps: the "133 blocked"
 figure was my own measurement error

Commit e0d69d1e30 landed 25 retractions and held back 133 as "blocked by a
second defect". That number was wrong, and an independent re-derivation found
why: I computed it with `lint_artifact` -- the RAW validator, which lints any
file handed to it -- while the pre-commit hook runs `lint_paths`, which SKIPS
non-candidates first. Of the 158 eligible artifacts, 141 are not ARC candidates
at all, so the hook never inspects them and never refused them. My stated reason
for holding them back did not survive contact with the thing that actually
refuses commits.

Measured with the hook's own path this time: 123 landable, 8 genuinely refused.
That matches the reviewer's independent count almost exactly.

Every artifact was re-verified INDIVIDUALLY at write time rather than trusting
the earlier sweep: 0 of the 131 carried a live CRITICAL flag. The two the
reviewer warned about -- exp4691 (TAUTOLOGY) and exp4716
(LEVER_EXERCISE_EVIDENCE_DEGENERATE), whose stamps are NOT stale -- are not in
this eligible set, so nothing here touches them.

The 8 hook-refused artifacts were restored to their stamped state rather than
landed half-corrected. experiment_5895 is mode 444, a deliberate
write-protection, and was skipped rather than chmod-ed: 123 = 122 committed + 1
read-only.

Retraction follows the route determination_preservation_lint.py documents: keep
the field, set it false, add flagged_adversarial_cleared_note beside it.
Verified before commit: flagged_adversarial absent from 0 artifacts, every
corrigendum_pending preserved, determination-preservation-lint OK, arc-artifact
lint exit 0 on the staged set, and every staged path checked against my own list
-- zero strays, which matters because the index is shared with three other
agents and swallowed thirteen of another agent's paths earlier today.

Total retracted across both commits: 147 of 158 eligible. Still deliberately
untouched: the 19 IMPLAUSIBLE_PERFECT, 9 no-reason and 15 mixed-kind stamps,
which have per-artifact recommendations from the review and must never be swept
-- three of the "no reason" stamps turned out to have substantive documented
reasons living in commit messages rather than artifacts.

